course: dictionary
lesson: 13377
title: Word detective: haywire
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words look like they are made of smaller words that do not help you. «Haywire» has hay and wire in it, but you do not need a farm to understand it. Read the words around it to find its meaning.
explain: «My tablet went haywire and started switching apps by itself.» Went, switching and by itself are the clues. Something that should be working is acting strangely and out of control, so haywire means out of control.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «My tablet was out of control and started switching apps by itself.» It still makes sense, so you have it right. You can also use haywire for people and plans: «Our plans went haywire when the bus broke down.»
fact: «Haywire» means out of control or not working properly.
fact: «Haywire» is informal, so you hear it in chatty speech and stories more than in formal writing.
fact: The word comes from wire used to tie hay bales, which could get tangled easily.
fact: Common phrases are go haywire and everything went haywire.
fact: For a person or plan, «haywire» means crazy or messed up.
exercise: «The traffic lights went haywire, and every light turned green at once.» What does haywire mean here? | *Out of control, not working properly | Very slow and calm | Shiny and new | Covered in hay
exercise: Dad says, «Our holiday plans went haywire when the flight was cancelled.» What does it mean? | The plans were made of wire | *The plans became messed up | The plans were tidy and organised | The plans were finished early
exercise: Which phrase means the same as the computer went haywire? | *The computer started behaving wildly and not working properly | The computer was switched off for a rest | The computer was given a new screen | The computer ran slowly and calmly
test: «After the storm, the garden sprinkler went haywire and sprayed the cat.» What does haywire suggest about the sprinkler? | None, you need a dictionary | It was very quiet and still | Which words are the clues? | The word storm only | The words went and sprayed the cat | *It was acting strangely, out of control | It was working perfectly | The word garden only | It was made of hay
test: Mia says, «Everything went haywire at the school disco when the music stopped and the lights kept flashing.» Which is the best swap for haywire? | Went very quickly into the hall | Went outside | Went to sleep | *Went out of control
exam: «The robot went haywire and started dancing across the kitchen.» What does haywire mean? | Covered in hay | Clean and tidy | *Out of control, not working properly | Quiet and calm | Very tired and sleepy
